+## Relationship kinds (2026-10-05 — plan [2026-10-05-ucpcomponent-move-ior-package](plans/2026-10-05-ucpcomponent-move-ior-package.md))
+
+Relationships are UNITS (`RelationshipModel`, each with its uuid), never strings. The kinds that place and connect components:
+
+| Kind | Meaning | Multiplicity | Navigation |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `containedBy` (role-less) | this class is a UNIT of another component (lives in its folder) | 0..1 | one way |
+| **`packagedIn`** | this COMPONENT is a sub-component of another, which is therefore a Package (Tron, [ucp.md](ucp.md) P) | **exactly one placement fact per component**, 0..1 target | one way; the namespace is DERIVED from it |
+| **`dependency`** | what this class depends on — a Thinglish collection | 0..n | **BIDIRECTIONAL** (Tron: *"it should be bidirectional navigatable and therefore it needs to be modeled as a bidirectional relationship in the MDA M3, M2 tree"*) |
+
+- **One fact, two navigations.** A `dependency` is stored ONCE (on the depending class); its opposite end — the class's **dependants** — is DERIVED, never stored twice. At M3 `M3Relationship.opposite` derives the opposite end; at M2 `M2AbstractDependency extends M2AbstractCollection` (a dependency IS a collection) and answers its dependants.
+- **Facts are location-free.** A `dependency` names CLASSES, never paths: so a `move()` rewrites no dependant, and generate re-derives every import specifier from the layout (eamd-ucp rule 8).
+- **`packagedIn` has a deterministic identity.** A component has ONE placement, so the fact's uuid is name-derived from the component's own uuid + `packagedIn` by ONE catalogued class that owns deterministic identity — never random (two equal moves must be byte-identical), never derived from the target (a move changes the target, not the identity).
+
